# Every 5 min: one `heartbeat` row per 'status services' line in the sd
# database, the Health page's and the Usage flags' feed (system sd:9259):
# status (ok, degraded, outage, unknown), open incidents and read time.
# A failed read stores `unknown`, never `ok`. The list is the setting row
# dashboard.status_services (Settings); a store that never held it
# starts with the services the operator chose on 2026-11-17.
# Hub only: the rows go to the hub's database. A refused list line is an
# SD_REPORT_ATTENTION line; a store that does not open exits 1.
# SD_PACK_ROOT is escaped so the `bash -c` that runs the command reads it,
# after ~/.config/shell/env.sh; this file is sourced before env.sh is.
JOB_SCHEDULE="*/5 * * * *"
JOB_TIMEOUT="4m"
JOB_COMMAND="\"\${SD_PACK_ROOT:-\$HOME/repos/platypeeps/sd-workflow}/.venv/bin/python\" \"$ROOT/../local-agent-meter/agent-meter.py\" services"
JOB_DIR="$ROOT/../local-agent-meter"
JOB_PROMPT=""
JOB_MODEL=""
JOB_CLAUDE_ARGS=""
